[?2004h> # BILL-212 release summary
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> The calendar clamped every renewal to the 28th and then calculated the next
[?2004l[?2004h> renewal from that shortened date. Proration also assumed 30/365-day periods,
[?2004l[?2004h> credited the old plan at the change-date price, and prorated interval changes
[?2004l[?2004h> instead of starting a full new billing cycle.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Changes:
[?2004l[?2004h> - Clamp to the target month's actual last day, including leap years.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Calculate cycle boundaries directly from the original anchor, in constant time.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Use actual cycle days and the old price in force at cycle start.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Keep the anchor for same-interval changes; charge full price and re-anchor on
[?2004l[?2004h>   the change date for monthly/annual switches.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Round exact integer ratios half-to-even, without Decimal-context precision loss.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Add calendar, rounding, and end-to-end CLI regression tests.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Validation: `python -m unittest discover -s tests` passes all 26 tests, including
[?2004l[?2004h> bulk repricing within the unchanged 0.2-second budget. All 10 finance worked
[?2004l[?2004h> examples are checked through `python -m billing preview`, including negative
[?2004l[?2004h> totals carried as account credit. Public API signatures are unchanged. No known
[?2004l[?2004h> failures were added, and existing fixtures, data, and release controls are unchanged.
